{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788347529973,"sessionID":"ses_f9e2e5412ffeyD0ZjwOyLPIQbA","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_a57aedbe53e14155922706e6","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/workers/.scratch/20260902_140812/mish-generate/task.md"},"output":"<path>/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/workers/.scratch/20260902_140812/mish-generate/task.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: You are implementing ONE operator for the CANN Bench benchmark (https://gitcode.com/cann/cann-bench) as a pyasc asc2 JIT kernel module targeting an Ascend 950PR NPU. You have NO NPU access — the official harness evaluates your file on real hardware after you finish. Score per operator = 0.2 compile + 0.3 accuracy (all 20 cases must pass a relative-error check against golden.py) + 0.5 performance (profiler-measured kernel time vs an aclnn baseline).\n2: \n3: # Task\n4: \n5: Operator: **Mish**. Write the file `candidate.py` in the current working directory: a complete Python module whose public callable `mish` implements the schema below. Nothing else — no tests, no other files.\n6: \n7: # Operator specification\n8: \n9: ## desc.md\n10: \n11: # Mish 算子 API 描述\n12: \n13: ## 1. 算子简介\n14: \n15: Mish 是一种自正则化的非单调神经网络激活函数，具有平滑、非单调的特性，在部分场景下性能优于 ReLU 和 Swish。\n16: \n17: **主要应用场景**：\n18: - YOLOv4/v5 等目标检测模型的激活层\n19: - 深层卷积网络中替代 ReLU 的激活函数\n20: - 需要平滑梯度的深度学习模型\n21: \n22: **算子特征**：\n23: - 难度等级：L1（Elementwise）\n24: - 单输入单输出，逐元素运算，输出 shape 与输入完全一致\n25: - 支持 0~8 维输入\n26: \n27: ## 2. 算子定义\n28: \n29: ### 数学公式\n30: \n31: $$\n32: y = x \\cdot \\tanh(\\text{softplus}(x)) = x \\cdot \\tanh(\\ln(1 + e^x))\n33: $$\n34: \n35: ### 特殊情况\n36: \n37: | 输入 | 输出 |\n38: |------|------|\n39: | x = 0 | y = 0 |\n40: | x → +∞ | y → x（趋近恒等） |\n41: | x → -∞ | y → 0 |\n42: \n43: ## 3. 接口规范\n44: \n45: ### 算子原型\n46: \n47: ```python\n48: cann_bench.mish(Tensor x) -> Tensor y\n49: ```\n50: \n51: ### 输入参数说明\n52: \n53: | 参数 | 类型 | 默认值 | 描述 |\n54: |------|------|--------|------|\n55: | x | Tensor | 必选 | 输入张量，支持 0~8 维 |\n56: \n57: ### 输出\n58: \n59: | 参数 | Shape | dtype | 描述 |\n60: |------|-------|-------|------|\n61: | y | 与输入 x 相同 | 与输入 x 相同 | Mish 激活结果 |\n62: \n63: ### 数据类型\n64: \n65: | 输入 dtype | 输出 dtype |\n66: |-----------|-----------|\n67: | float16 | float16 |\n68: | float32 | float32 |\n69: | bfloat16 | bfloat16 |\n70: \n71: ### 规则与约束\n72: \n73: - 输出 shape 与输入 shape 完全一致，输出 dtype 与输入 dtype 一致\n74: - 无额外属性参数\n75: \n76: ### 支持范围\n77: \n78: 输入 tensor 各维度与参数的支持范围：\n79: \n80: | 维度 / 参数 | 范围 | 备注 |\n81: |---|---|---|\n82: | `x` 维度数 (ndim) | 1 ~ 8 | cases.csv 实测 1 ~ 5 |\n83: | `x` 单维大小 | 1 ~ 16384 | cases.csv 实测 2 ~ 8193 |\n84: | `x` 总元素数 | 1 ~ 64M | cases.csv 实测 ~1M ~ 64M  |\n85: \n86: 约束：输出 shape 与输入 shape 完全一致，无 broadcasting；无额外属性。\n87: \n88: ## 4. 精度要求\n89: \n90: 采用[生态算子精度标准](https://gitcode.com/cann/opbase/blob/master/docs/zh/ops_precision_standard/experimental_standard.md)进行验证。\n91: \n92: **误差指标**：\n93: \n94: 1. 平均相对误差（MERE）：采样点中相对误差平均值\n95: \n96:    $$\n97:    \\text{MERE} = \\text{avg}(\\frac{\\text{abs}(actual - golden)}{\\text{abs}(golden)+\\text{1e-7}})\n98:    $$\n99: \n100: 2. 最大相对误差（MARE）：采样点中相对误差最大值\n101: \n102:    $$\n103:    \\text{MARE} = \\max(\\frac{\\text{abs}(actual - golden)}{\\text{abs}(golden)+\\text{1e-7}})\n104:    $$\n105: \n106: **通过标准**：\n107: \n108: | 数据类型 | FLOAT16 | BFLOAT16 | FLOAT32 | HiFLOAT32 | FLOAT8 E4M3 | FLOAT8 E5M2 |\n109: |----------|---------|----------|---------|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n110: | **通过阈值(Threshold)** | 2^-10 | 2^-7 | 2^-13 | 2^-11 | 2^-3 | 2^-2 |\n111: \n112: 当平均相对误差 MERE < Threshold，最大相对误差 MARE < 10 * Threshold 时判定为通过。\n113: \n114: \n115: ## 5. 标准 Golden 代码\n116: \n117: ```python\n118: import torch\n119: \n120: def mish(\n121:     x: torch.Tensor\n122: ) -> torch.Tensor:\n123:     \"\"\"\n124:     自正则化的非单调神经网络激活函数\n125: \n126:     公式: y = x * tanh(softplus(x))\n127: \n128:     Args:\n129:         x: 输入张量\n130: \n131:     Returns:\n132:         输出张量，Mish激活结果\n133:     \"\"\"\n134:     return torch.nn.functional.mish(x)\n135: ```\n136: \n137: ## 6. 额外信息\n138: \n139: ### 算子调用示例\n140: \n141: ```python\n142: import torch\n143: import cann_bench\n144: \n145: x = torch.randn(1024, 1024, dtype=torch.float32, device=\"npu\")\n146: y = cann_bench.mish(x)\n147: ```\n148: \n149: ## proto.yaml\n150: \n151: ```yaml\n152: operator:\n153:   name: Mish\n154:   category: Elementwise\n155:   difficulty: L1\n156:   formula: y = x * tanh(softplus(x))\n157:   description: 自正则化的非单调神经网络激活函数\n158:   shape_support: 输入0-8维\n159:   attrs: []\n160:   inputs:\n161:   - name: x\n162:     description: 输入张量\n163:     dtype:\n164:     - float16\n165:     - float32\n166:     - bfloat16\n167:   outputs:\n168:   - name: y\n169:     description: 输出张量，Mish激活结果\n170:     dtype:\n171:     - float16\n172:     - float32\n173:     - bfloat16\n174:   schema: mish(Tensor x) -> Tensor y\n175: ```\n176: \n177: ## golden.py — reference semantics ONLY (you must NOT compute with torch like this; reimplement the math in asc2 kernels)\n178: \n179: ```python\n180: #!/usr/bin/python3\n181: # coding=utf-8\n182: \n183: \n184: import torch\n185: \n186: \"\"\"\n187: Mish算子Torch Golden参考实现\n188: \n189: 自正则化的非单调神经网络激活函数\n190: 公式: y = x * tanh(softplus(x))\n191: \"\"\"\n192: def mish(\n193:     x: torch.Tensor\n194: ) -> torch.Tensor:\n195:     \"\"\"\n196:     自正则化的非单调神经网络激活函数\n197: \n198:     公式: y = x * tanh(softplus(x))\n199: \n200:     Args:\n201:         x: 输入张量\n202: \n203:     Returns:\n204:         输出张量，Mish激活结果\n205:     \"\"\"\n206:     return torch.nn.functional.mish(x)\n207: ```\n208: \n209: ## Evaluation cases your module must handle (shapes, dtypes, value ranges, attrs)\n210: \n211: | case | shapes | dtype | value_range | attrs |\n212: |---|---|---|---|---|\n213: | 1 | [[1024, 1024]] | ['float16'] | [-1, 1] | - |\n214: | 2 | [[2048, 2048]] | ['float32'] | [-2, 2] | - |\n215: | 3 | [[4096, 4096]] | ['bfloat16'] | [-3, 3] | - |\n216: | 4 | [[8192, 8192]] | ['float16'] | [-10, 10] | - |\n217: | 5 | [[8192, 8192]] | ['float32'] | [-100, 100] | - |\n218: | 6 | [[1023, 1023]] | ['bfloat16'] | [-0.1, 0.1] | - |\n219: | 7 | [[1009, 1021]] | ['float16'] | [-1, 2] | - |\n220: | 8 | [[1537, 769]] | ['float32'] | [-5, 10] | - |\n221: | 9 | [[363, 367, 373]] | ['bfloat16'] | [-50, 100] | - |\n222: | 10 | [[2049, 513]] | ['float16'] | [-65504, 65504] | - |\n223: | 11 | [[3, 7, 13, 4001]] | ['float32'] | [-88, 88] | - |\n224: | 12 | [[1000003]] | ['bfloat16'] | [-inf, inf] | - |\n225: | 13 | [[11, 13, 17, 67, 67]] | ['float32'] | [nan, nan] | - |\n226: | 14 | [[3, 7, 11, 13, 1009]] | ['float16'] | [0, 0] | - |\n227: | 15 | [[512, 2049]] | ['float32'] | [-0.5, 0.5] | - |\n228: | 16 | [[255, 8193]] | ['bfloat16'] | [-1, 3] | - |\n229: | 17 | [[4097, 511]] | ['float16'] | [-1000, 1000] | - |\n230: | 18 | [[2, 511, 2049]] | ['float32'] | [-0.2, 0.2] | - |\n231: | 19 | [[4, 255, 2049]] | ['bfloat16'] | [-3, 6] | - |\n232: | 20 | [[2, 3, 17, 1024, 101]] | ['float32'] | [-20, 40] | - |\n233: \n234: # Reference module — sigmoid.py from this submission (structure to copy; it scores 100% accuracy on this harness)\n235: \n236: ```python\n237: \"\"\"CANN Bench Sigmoid interface implemented as a pyasc asc2 kernel.\n238: \n239: Kernel design (pyasc-api-patterns Pattern A, grid-stride variant):\n240:   - 1-D flatten; each block strides over tiles so any element count works.\n241:   - Tail tiles handled with ``real_shape`` loads/stores (no host padding).\n242:   - f16/bf16 inputs are promoted to f32 inside the kernel for precision\n243:     (the spec's precision standard expects f32 internal compute).\n244:   - Host selects between two compiled tile sizes: a wide tile (3072) when\n245:     the element count fills all 72 cores, otherwise a narrow tile (1024) to\n246:     maximize core utilization on small shapes.\n247:   - sigmoid(x) = 1 / (1 + e^(-x)); IEEE saturation gives the correct\n248:     limits at extreme inputs (e^inf -> inf -> y=0, e^-inf -> 0 -> y=1).\n249: \"\"\"\n250: \n251: import torch\n252: \n253: import asc\n254: import asc2\n255: \n256: from ._pyasc_runtime import ensure_npu_platform\n257: \n258: _WIDE_TILE = 3072\n259: _NARROW_TILE = 1024\n260: _MAX_CORES = 72\n261: \n262: \n263: @asc2.jit\n264: def _sigmoid_kernel(x_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress, out_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n265:                     size: int, num_tiles: int, tile_size: asc.ConstExpr[int]):\n266:     x_gm = asc2.global_tensor(x_ptr, [size])\n267:     out_gm = asc2.global_tensor(out_ptr, [size])\n268:     for t in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(),\n269:                         unroll_factor=2):\n270:         off = t * tile_size\n271:         n = tile_size if off + tile_size <= size else size - off\n272:         x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])\n273:         xf = x.to(asc.float32)\n274:         y = asc2.div(1.0, asc2.exp(-xf) + 1.0)\n275:         asc2.copy_out(y.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])\n276: \n277: \n278: def sigmoid(x: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n279:     \"\"\"Element-wise sigmoid of an NPU tensor via a pyasc asc2 kernel.\"\"\"\n280:     ensure_npu_platform()\n281:     if not x.is_contiguous():\n282:         x = x.contiguous()\n283:     out = torch.empty_like(x)\n284:     size = x.numel()\n285:     if size == 0:\n286:         return out\n287:     if size >= _MAX_CORES * _WIDE_TILE:\n288:         num_tiles = asc.ceildiv(size, _WIDE_TILE)\n289:         cores = min(_MAX_CORES, num_tiles)\n290:         _sigmoid_kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, _WIDE_TILE)\n291:     else:\n292:         num_tiles = asc.ceildiv(size, _NARROW_TILE)\n293:         cores = min(_MAX_CORES, num_tiles)\n294:         _sigmoid_kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, _NARROW_TILE)\n295:     return out\n296: \n297: ```\n298: \n299: # pyasc asc2 kernel contract (follow EXACTLY — every rule below was learned from real failures on this hardware)\n300: \n301: ## Module shape\n302: \n303: Your file becomes `cann_bench/<module>.py` inside the submission wheel. It must contain:\n304: \n305: - imports at module top: `import torch`, `import asc`, `import asc2`,\n306:   `from ._pyasc_runtime import ensure_npu_platform` (and `import math` if needed)\n307: - one or more `@asc2.jit` kernel functions\n308: - ONE public callable matching the operator schema exactly (name and signature)\n309: - wrapper body: call `ensure_npu_platform()` first; make inputs contiguous if\n310:   needed (`x = x.contiguous()` is allowed); allocate outputs with\n311:   `torch.empty_like(x)` or `torch.empty(shape, dtype=..., device=x.device)`;\n312:   launch `kernel[cores](tensor_args..., int_args..., float_args..., constexpr_args...)`;\n313:   return contiguous NPU tensor(s)\n314: \n315: ## Kernel authoring rules\n316: \n317: - Global memory views: `asc2.global_tensor(ptr, [size])` (1-D) or\n318:   `asc2.global_tensor(ptr, [rows, cols])` (2-D). Ranks of global_tensor /\n319:   copy_in / copy_out / offsets must ALL match — never mix 1-D and 2-D.\n320: - Kernel params: pointers typed `asc.GlobalAddress`; sizes as plain `int`\n321:   (runtime); tile sizes as `asc.ConstExpr[int]` (compile-time; REQUIRED for any\n322:   value used inside a copy_in tile shape); scalars as `float`.\n323: - Grid-stride tile loop (the proven pattern):\n324: \n325: ```python\n326: for t in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(), unroll_factor=2):\n327:     off = t * tile_size\n328:     n = tile_size if off + tile_size <= size else size - off   # tail handling\n329:     x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])\n330:     ...compute on tiles...\n331:     asc2.copy_out(y.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])\n332: ```\n333: \n334: - Launch: `kernel[cores](...)` with `cores = min(72, num_tiles)` (72 AIV cores\n335:   on this 950PR box). No stream argument.\n336: - Available tile ops: `+ - * /` (tile-tile and tile-scalar), `asc2.abs`,\n337:   `asc2.exp`, `asc2.exp2`, `asc2.log`, `asc2.log2`, `asc2.sqrt`,\n338:   `asc2.rsqrt`, `asc2.tanh`, `asc2.erf`, `asc2.sin`, `asc2.cos`,\n339:   `asc2.floor`, `asc2.ceil`, `asc2.relu`, `asc2.maximum`, `asc2.minimum`,\n340:   comparisons (`x >= 0.0`, `asc2.less(a, b)`, ... — NO int64 operands),\n341:   `asc2.where(cond, a, b)`, `asc2.reduce_sum(x)`, `asc2.reduce_max(x)`,\n342:   `asc2.reduce_min(x)`, `asc2.full([shape], scalar, dtype=...)`,\n343:   `asc2.cast(tile, dtype)` / `tile.to(dtype)` casts, integer\n344:   `asc2.left_shift`/`asc2.right_shift`, tile-shape ops `asc2.reshape`,\n345:   `asc2.transpose`, `asc2.ravel`, `asc2.expand_dims`, `asc2.squeeze`,\n346:   `asc2.broadcast_to`, `asc2.concat`, unary `-x`.\n347: - int8 tiles: loading (copy_in) is fine but NO vector op accepts int8 input\n348:   (not even `.to`); convert with `asc2.cast(t, asc.float16)` first. There is\n349:   no uint8 tile dtype at all.\n350: - Scalars go on the RIGHT of tile arithmetic (Tile has no `__rmul__`):\n351:   write `x * 0.5`, NEVER `0.5 * x`. Same for `+ - /`.\n352: - f16/bf16 inputs: promote to f32 in-kernel (`xf = x.to(asc.float32)`),\n353:   compute in f32, cast back on copy_out (`y.to(x.dtype)`).\n354: - UB (unified buffer) budget: ~253952 bytes total under static allocation.\n355:   Every distinct f32 tile value costs `4 * TILE` bytes, `unroll_factor=2`\n356:   doubles the total, and the compiler adds hidden temporaries — MEASURED\n357:   calibration: the sigmoid chain (f16 load, f32 cast, `-x`, `exp`, `+1`,\n358:   `div`, f16 store ≈ 6 visible values) uses 155648 bytes at TILE=2048 and\n359:   311296 (OVERFLOW) at TILE=4096, i.e. real usage ≈ 1.6x the naive\n360:   `visible_values * 4 * TILE * 2` estimate. Budget with that 1.6x factor.\n361:   Rule of thumb: TILE=2048 for short chains (< 8 values), 1024 for medium,\n362:   512 for long (> 16). A launch failing with `RuntimeError: UB overflow: X\n363:   bytes are available, Y bytes are used` means: halve TILE (do NOT drop\n364:   cases).\n365: - `asc2.where` / comparison destination tiles must be a multiple of 256 bytes\n366:   (`TILE * 4 % 256 == 0` for f32 — any TILE >= 64 is safe).\n367: - Loop-carried scalar accumulators (VERIFIED on this build): seed with\n368:   `acc = asc2.reduce_sum(asc2.full([1, 64], 0.0, dtype=asc.float32))`\n369:   (a bare `acc = 0.0` fails codegen with \"re-assigned to an object with\n370:   different type\"), then `acc = acc + asc2.reduce_sum(x)` inside a plain\n371:   `asc2.range(...)` loop. `asc2.range` accepts ONLY `unroll_factor` and\n372:   `parallel` — there is NO `gm_barrier` kwarg on this build (it raises\n373:   TypeError).\n374: - Cross-core reductions (VERIFIED): `asc2.atomic_add(src_tile, dst_gm,\n375:   [offset])` atomically accumulates a tile into global memory (dtypes int16/\n376:   int32/f16/bf16/f32; also `asc2.atomic_max`). Host must zero the\n377:   destination first (`torch.zeros(...)` — tensor creation is allowed).\n378:   Pattern: each core reduce_sums its tiles into a scalar, widens it with\n379:   `asc2.full([8], s, dtype=...)`, and atomic_adds slot [0]; a second tiny\n380:   kernel (or the same one on one core) applies any final transform.\n381: - Scalar reduction results must be widened before store:\n382:   `asc2.copy_out(asc2.full([8], s, dtype=...), out_gm, [0], real_shape=[8])`\n383:   style (min 32 bytes).\n384: - Inside `@asc2.jit`: NO `print`, NO imports, NO `break`/`continue`/early\n385:   `return`, NO exceptions, NO Python `range()` over runtime values (use\n386:   `asc2.range`), NO `math.*` calls (precompute module-level constants).\n387: \n388: ## Numerical stability (MANDATORY — f32 cases use ranges like [-88, 88] and [-100, 100] under a ~1.2e-4 relative-error threshold)\n389: \n390: - Never let `exp()` see a positive argument that can overflow; never subtract\n391:   nearly-equal quantities (catastrophic cancellation); never rely on\n392:   `log(1 + tiny)` (flushes to 0 below tiny < 6e-8).\n393: - Proven cancellation-free building blocks (all verified on this harness):\n394:   - `sigmoid(s) = exp(min(s, 0)) / (1 + exp(-|s|))`\n395:   - `1 + tanh(u) = 2 * sigmoid(2u)`\n396:   - `tanh(softplus(x))`: with `w = exp(-|x|)`, equals\n397:     `(1 + 2w) / (1 + 2w + 2w^2)` for `x >= 0`, `(w^2 + 2w) / (w^2 + 2w + 2)`\n398:     for `x < 0` (exact identities; blend with `asc2.where(xf >= 0.0, ...)`)\n399:   - `erfc(z)` for `z >= 0`: Numerical Recipes fit `t * exp(-z*z + P(t))`,\n400:     `t = 1/(1 + z/2)`, rel. err < 1.2e-7 (see the gelu reference module for\n401:     the 9-coefficient Horner chain)\n402: - IEEE special values (inf/nan scalars or extreme inputs) propagate correctly\n403:   through the hardware ops — do NOT special-case them with host branches\n404:   unless the golden does.\n405: \n406: ## Anti-cheat (violations zero the submission)\n407: \n408: - ALL numerical work happens inside `@asc2.jit` kernels launched on the NPU.\n409: - torch usage is allowed ONLY for: output allocation (`torch.empty`,\n410:   `torch.empty_like`), metadata (`.shape`, `.numel()`, `.stride()`, `.dtype`,\n411:   `.is_contiguous()`), contiguity (`.contiguous()`), and views (`.view`,\n412:   `.reshape`, `.narrow`, indexing that returns a view).\n413: - FORBIDDEN anywhere in the module: torch math/compute ops (`torch.mul`,\n414:   `torch.norm`, `torch.nn.functional.*`, tensor arithmetic like `a + b`,\n415:   `x.sigmoid()`, `.to(dtype)` casts of device data, `torch.cat`,\n416:   `torch.clone`, `torch.sum`, ...). The harness hooks torch dispatch and\n417:   rotates input data pointers between calls — caching outputs by `data_ptr`\n418:   is detected and scored as cheating.\n419: - Outputs must be contiguous NPU tensors with exactly the golden's\n420:   shape/dtype. Do not return views of inputs.\n421: \n422: \n423: # Operator-specific guidance\n424: \n425: -\n426: \n427: # Deliverable\n428: \n429: Write ONLY `candidate.py` (complete, self-contained module). Public callable named exactly `mish` with the exact schema signature including attr defaults. Think hard about numerical stability across the full value ranges listed above, and about the UB budget for your op chain before picking TILE.\n430: \n431: IMPORTANT — no local execution: pyasc/asc/asc2/torch_npu are NOT installed on this machine and there is no NPU here. Do NOT run, import, compile-check, or test your code, and do not install packages — any such attempt wastes your entire time budget. Reason statically, write `candidate.py`, optionally run `python3 -m py_compile candidate.py` (syntax only), then STOP and reply DONE.\n\n(End of file - total 431 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"You are implementing ONE operator for the CANN Bench benchmark (https://gitcode.com/cann/cann-bench) as a pyasc asc2 JIT kernel module targeting an Ascend 950PR NPU. You have NO NPU access — the official harness evaluates your file on real hardware after you finish. Score per operator = 0.2 compile + 0.3 accuracy (all 20 cases must pass a relative-error check against golden.py) + 0.5 performance (profiler-measured kernel time vs an aclnn baseline).\n\n# Task\n\nOperator: **Mish**. Write the file `candidate.py` in the current working directory: a complete Python module whose public callable `mish` implements the schema below. Nothing else — no tests, no other files.\n\n# Operator specification\n\n## desc.md\n\n# Mish 算子 API 描述\n\n## 1. 算子简介\n\nMish 是一种自正则化的非单调神经网络激活函数，具有平滑、非单调的特性，在部分场景下性能优于 ReLU 和 Swish。\n\n**主要应用场景**：\n- YOLOv4/v5 等目标检测模型的激活层\n- 深层卷积网络中替代 ReLU 的激活函数\n- 需要平滑梯度的深度学习模型","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/workers/.scratch/20260902_140812/mish-generate/task.md","text":"You are implementing ONE operator for the CANN Bench benchmark (https://gitcode.com/cann/cann-bench) as a pyasc asc2 JIT kernel module targeting an Ascend 950PR NPU. You have NO NPU access — the official harness evaluates your file on real hardware after you finish. Score per operator = 0.2 compile + 0.3 accuracy (all 20 cases must pass a relative-error check against golden.py) + 0.5 performance (profiler-measured kernel time vs an aclnn baseline).\n\n# Task\n\nOperator: **Mish**. Write the file `candidate.py` in the current working directory: a complete Python module whose public callable `mish` implements the schema below. Nothing else — no tests, no other files.\n\n# Operator specification\n\n## desc.md\n\n# Mish 算子 API 描述\n\n## 1. 算子简介\n\nMish 是一种自正则化的非单调神经网络激活函数，具有平滑、非单调的特性，在部分场景下性能优于 ReLU 和 Swish。\n\n**主要应用场景**：\n- YOLOv4/v5 等目标检测模型的激活层\n- 深层卷积网络中替代 ReLU 的激活函数\n- 需要平滑梯度的深度学习模型\n\n**算子特征**：\n- 难度等级：L1（Elementwise）\n- 单输入单输出，逐元素运算，输出 shape 与输入完全一致\n- 支持 0~8 维输入\n\n## 2. 算子定义\n\n### 数学公式\n\n$$\ny = x \\cdot \\tanh(\\text{softplus}(x)) = x \\cdot \\tanh(\\ln(1 + e^x))\n$$\n\n### 特殊情况\n\n| 输入 | 输出 |\n|------|------|\n| x = 0 | y = 0 |\n| x → +∞ | y → x（趋近恒等） |\n| x → -∞ | y → 0 |\n\n## 3. 接口规范\n\n### 算子原型\n\n```python\ncann_bench.mish(Tensor x) -> Tensor y\n```\n\n### 输入参数说明\n\n| 参数 | 类型 | 默认值 | 描述 |\n|------|------|--------|------|\n| x | Tensor | 必选 | 输入张量，支持 0~8 维 |\n\n### 输出\n\n| 参数 | Shape | dtype | 描述 |\n|------|-------|-------|------|\n| y | 与输入 x 相同 | 与输入 x 相同 | Mish 激活结果 |\n\n### 数据类型\n\n| 输入 dtype | 输出 dtype |\n|-----------|-----------|\n| float16 | float16 |\n| float32 | float32 |\n| bfloat16 | bfloat16 |\n\n### 规则与约束\n\n- 输出 shape 与输入 shape 完全一致，输出 dtype 与输入 dtype 一致\n- 无额外属性参数\n\n### 支持范围\n\n输入 tensor 各维度与参数的支持范围：\n\n| 维度 / 参数 | 范围 | 备注 |\n|---|---|---|\n| `x` 维度数 (ndim) | 1 ~ 8 | cases.csv 实测 1 ~ 5 |\n| `x` 单维大小 | 1 ~ 16384 | cases.csv 实测 2 ~ 8193 |\n| `x` 总元素数 | 1 ~ 64M | cases.csv 实测 ~1M ~ 64M  |\n\n约束：输出 shape 与输入 shape 完全一致，无 broadcasting；无额外属性。\n\n## 4. 精度要求\n\n采用[生态算子精度标准](https://gitcode.com/cann/opbase/blob/master/docs/zh/ops_precision_standard/experimental_standard.md)进行验证。\n\n**误差指标**：\n\n1. 平均相对误差（MERE）：采样点中相对误差平均值\n\n   $$\n   \\text{MERE} = \\text{avg}(\\frac{\\text{abs}(actual - golden)}{\\text{abs}(golden)+\\text{1e-7}})\n   $$\n\n2. 最大相对误差（MARE）：采样点中相对误差最大值\n\n   $$\n   \\text{MARE} = \\max(\\frac{\\text{abs}(actual - golden)}{\\text{abs}(golden)+\\text{1e-7}})\n   $$\n\n**通过标准**：\n\n| 数据类型 | FLOAT16 | BFLOAT16 | FLOAT32 | HiFLOAT32 | FLOAT8 E4M3 | FLOAT8 E5M2 |\n|----------|---------|----------|---------|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| **通过阈值(Threshold)** | 2^-10 | 2^-7 | 2^-13 | 2^-11 | 2^-3 | 2^-2 |\n\n当平均相对误差 MERE < Threshold，最大相对误差 MARE < 10 * Threshold 时判定为通过。\n\n\n## 5. 标准 Golden 代码\n\n```python\nimport torch\n\ndef mish(\n    x: torch.Tensor\n) -> torch.Tensor:\n    \"\"\"\n    自正则化的非单调神经网络激活函数\n\n    公式: y = x * tanh(softplus(x))\n\n    Args:\n        x: 输入张量\n\n    Returns:\n        输出张量，Mish激活结果\n    \"\"\"\n    return torch.nn.functional.mish(x)\n```\n\n## 6. 额外信息\n\n### 算子调用示例\n\n```python\nimport torch\nimport cann_bench\n\nx = torch.randn(1024, 1024, dtype=torch.float32, device=\"npu\")\ny = cann_bench.mish(x)\n```\n\n## proto.yaml\n\n```yaml\noperator:\n  name: Mish\n  category: Elementwise\n  difficulty: L1\n  formula: y = x * tanh(softplus(x))\n  description: 自正则化的非单调神经网络激活函数\n  shape_support: 输入0-8维\n  attrs: []\n  inputs:\n  - name: x\n    description: 输入张量\n    dtype:\n    - float16\n    - float32\n    - bfloat16\n  outputs:\n  - name: y\n    description: 输出张量，Mish激活结果\n    dtype:\n    - float16\n    - float32\n    - bfloat16\n  schema: mish(Tensor x) -> Tensor y\n```\n\n## golden.py — reference semantics ONLY (you must NOT compute with torch like this; reimplement the math in asc2 kernels)\n\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/python3\n# coding=utf-8\n\n\nimport torch\n\n\"\"\"\nMish算子Torch Golden参考实现\n\n自正则化的非单调神经网络激活函数\n公式: y = x * tanh(softplus(x))\n\"\"\"\ndef mish(\n    x: torch.Tensor\n) -> torch.Tensor:\n    \"\"\"\n    自正则化的非单调神经网络激活函数\n\n    公式: y = x * tanh(softplus(x))\n\n    Args:\n        x: 输入张量\n\n    Returns:\n        输出张量，Mish激活结果\n    \"\"\"\n    return torch.nn.functional.mish(x)\n```\n\n## Evaluation cases your module must handle (shapes, dtypes, value ranges, attrs)\n\n| case | shapes | dtype | value_range | attrs |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | [[1024, 1024]] | ['float16'] | [-1, 1] | - |\n| 2 | [[2048, 2048]] | ['float32'] | [-2, 2] | - |\n| 3 | [[4096, 4096]] | ['bfloat16'] | [-3, 3] | - |\n| 4 | [[8192, 8192]] | ['float16'] | [-10, 10] | - |\n| 5 | [[8192, 8192]] | ['float32'] | [-100, 100] | - |\n| 6 | [[1023, 1023]] | ['bfloat16'] | [-0.1, 0.1] | - |\n| 7 | [[1009, 1021]] | ['float16'] | [-1, 2] | - |\n| 8 | [[1537, 769]] | ['float32'] | [-5, 10] | - |\n| 9 | [[363, 367, 373]] | ['bfloat16'] | [-50, 100] | - |\n| 10 | [[2049, 513]] | ['float16'] | [-65504, 65504] | - |\n| 11 | [[3, 7, 13, 4001]] | ['float32'] | [-88, 88] | - |\n| 12 | [[1000003]] | ['bfloat16'] | [-inf, inf] | - |\n| 13 | [[11, 13, 17, 67, 67]] | ['float32'] | [nan, nan] | - |\n| 14 | [[3, 7, 11, 13, 1009]] | ['float16'] | [0, 0] | - |\n| 15 | [[512, 2049]] | ['float32'] | [-0.5, 0.5] | - |\n| 16 | [[255, 8193]] | ['bfloat16'] | [-1, 3] | - |\n| 17 | [[4097, 511]] | ['float16'] | [-1000, 1000] | - |\n| 18 | [[2, 511, 2049]] | ['float32'] | [-0.2, 0.2] | - |\n| 19 | [[4, 255, 2049]] | ['bfloat16'] | [-3, 6] | - |\n| 20 | [[2, 3, 17, 1024, 101]] | ['float32'] | [-20, 40] | - |\n\n# Reference module — sigmoid.py from this submission (structure to copy; it scores 100% accuracy on this harness)\n\n```python\n\"\"\"CANN Bench Sigmoid interface implemented as a pyasc asc2 kernel.\n\nKernel design (pyasc-api-patterns Pattern A, grid-stride variant):\n  - 1-D flatten; each block strides over tiles so any element count works.\n  - Tail tiles handled with ``real_shape`` loads/stores (no host padding).\n  - f16/bf16 inputs are promoted to f32 inside the kernel for precision\n    (the spec's precision standard expects f32 internal compute).\n  - Host selects between two compiled tile sizes: a wide tile (3072) when\n    the element count fills all 72 cores, otherwise a narrow tile (1024) to\n    maximize core utilization on small shapes.\n  - sigmoid(x) = 1 / (1 + e^(-x)); IEEE saturation gives the correct\n    limits at extreme inputs (e^inf -> inf -> y=0, e^-inf -> 0 -> y=1).\n\"\"\"\n\nimport torch\n\nimport asc\nimport asc2\n\nfrom ._pyasc_runtime import ensure_npu_platform\n\n_WIDE_TILE = 3072\n_NARROW_TILE = 1024\n_MAX_CORES = 72\n\n\n@asc2.jit\ndef _sigmoid_kernel(x_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress, out_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n                    size: int, num_tiles: int, tile_size: asc.ConstExpr[int]):\n    x_gm = asc2.global_tensor(x_ptr, [size])\n    out_gm = asc2.global_tensor(out_ptr, [size])\n    for t in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(),\n                        unroll_factor=2):\n        off = t * tile_size\n        n = tile_size if off + tile_size <= size else size - off\n        x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])\n        xf = x.to(asc.float32)\n        y = asc2.div(1.0, asc2.exp(-xf) + 1.0)\n        asc2.copy_out(y.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])\n\n\ndef sigmoid(x: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n    \"\"\"Element-wise sigmoid of an NPU tensor via a pyasc asc2 kernel.\"\"\"\n    ensure_npu_platform()\n    if not x.is_contiguous():\n        x = x.contiguous()\n    out = torch.empty_like(x)\n    size = x.numel()\n    if size == 0:\n        return out\n    if size >= _MAX_CORES * _WIDE_TILE:\n        num_tiles = asc.ceildiv(size, _WIDE_TILE)\n        cores = min(_MAX_CORES, num_tiles)\n        _sigmoid_kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, _WIDE_TILE)\n    else:\n        num_tiles = asc.ceildiv(size, _NARROW_TILE)\n        cores = min(_MAX_CORES, num_tiles)\n        _sigmoid_kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, _NARROW_TILE)\n    return out\n\n```\n\n# pyasc asc2 kernel contract (follow EXACTLY — every rule below was learned from real failures on this hardware)\n\n## Module shape\n\nYour file becomes `cann_bench/<module>.py` inside the submission wheel. It must contain:\n\n- imports at module top: `import torch`, `import asc`, `import asc2`,\n  `from ._pyasc_runtime import ensure_npu_platform` (and `import math` if needed)\n- one or more `@asc2.jit` kernel functions\n- ONE public callable matching the operator schema exactly (name and signature)\n- wrapper body: call `ensure_npu_platform()` first; make inputs contiguous if\n  needed (`x = x.contiguous()` is allowed); allocate outputs with\n  `torch.empty_like(x)` or `torch.empty(shape, dtype=..., device=x.device)`;\n  launch `kernel[cores](tensor_args..., int_args..., float_args..., constexpr_args...)`;\n  return contiguous NPU tensor(s)\n\n## Kernel authoring rules\n\n- Global memory views: `asc2.global_tensor(ptr, [size])` (1-D) or\n  `asc2.global_tensor(ptr, [rows, cols])` (2-D). Ranks of global_tensor /\n  copy_in / copy_out / offsets must ALL match — never mix 1-D and 2-D.\n- Kernel params: pointers typed `asc.GlobalAddress`; sizes as plain `int`\n  (runtime); tile sizes as `asc.ConstExpr[int]` (compile-time; REQUIRED for any\n  value used inside a copy_in tile shape); scalars as `float`.\n- Grid-stride tile loop (the proven pattern):\n\n```python\nfor t in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(), unroll_factor=2):\n    off = t * tile_size\n    n = tile_size if off + tile_size <= size else size - off   # tail handling\n    x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])\n    ...compute on tiles...\n    asc2.copy_out(y.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])\n```\n\n- Launch: `kernel[cores](...)` with `cores = min(72, num_tiles)` (72 AIV cores\n  on this 950PR box). No stream argument.\n- Available tile ops: `+ - * /` (tile-tile and tile-scalar), `asc2.abs`,\n  `asc2.exp`, `asc2.exp2`, `asc2.log`, `asc2.log2`, `asc2.sqrt`,\n  `asc2.rsqrt`, `asc2.tanh`, `asc2.erf`, `asc2.sin`, `asc2.cos`,\n  `asc2.floor`, `asc2.ceil`, `asc2.relu`, `asc2.maximum`, `asc2.minimum`,\n  comparisons (`x >= 0.0`, `asc2.less(a, b)`, ... — NO int64 operands),\n  `asc2.where(cond, a, b)`, `asc2.reduce_sum(x)`, `asc2.reduce_max(x)`,\n  `asc2.reduce_min(x)`, `asc2.full([shape], scalar, dtype=...)`,\n  `asc2.cast(tile, dtype)` / `tile.to(dtype)` casts, integer\n  `asc2.left_shift`/`asc2.right_shift`, tile-shape ops `asc2.reshape`,\n  `asc2.transpose`, `asc2.ravel`, `asc2.expand_dims`, `asc2.squeeze`,\n  `asc2.broadcast_to`, `asc2.concat`, unary `-x`.\n- int8 tiles: loading (copy_in) is fine but NO vector op accepts int8 input\n  (not even `.to`); convert with `asc2.cast(t, asc.float16)` first. There is\n  no uint8 tile dtype at all.\n- Scalars go on the RIGHT of tile arithmetic (Tile has no `__rmul__`):\n  write `x * 0.5`, NEVER `0.5 * x`. Same for `+ - /`.\n- f16/bf16 inputs: promote to f32 in-kernel (`xf = x.to(asc.float32)`),\n  compute in f32, cast back on copy_out (`y.to(x.dtype)`).\n- UB (unified buffer) budget: ~253952 bytes total under static allocation.\n  Every distinct f32 tile value costs `4 * TILE` bytes, `unroll_factor=2`\n  doubles the total, and the compiler adds hidden temporaries — MEASURED\n  calibration: the sigmoid chain (f16 load, f32 cast, `-x`, `exp`, `+1`,\n  `div`, f16 store ≈ 6 visible values) uses 155648 bytes at TILE=2048 and\n  311296 (OVERFLOW) at TILE=4096, i.e. real usage ≈ 1.6x the naive\n  `visible_values * 4 * TILE * 2` estimate. Budget with that 1.6x factor.\n  Rule of thumb: TILE=2048 for short chains (< 8 values), 1024 for medium,\n  512 for long (> 16). A launch failing with `RuntimeError: UB overflow: X\n  bytes are available, Y bytes are used` means: halve TILE (do NOT drop\n  cases).\n- `asc2.where` / comparison destination tiles must be a multiple of 256 bytes\n  (`TILE * 4 % 256 == 0` for f32 — any TILE >= 64 is safe).\n- Loop-carried scalar accumulators (VERIFIED on this build): seed with\n  `acc = asc2.reduce_sum(asc2.full([1, 64], 0.0, dtype=asc.float32))`\n  (a bare `acc = 0.0` fails codegen with \"re-assigned to an object with\n  different type\"), then `acc = acc + asc2.reduce_sum(x)` inside a plain\n  `asc2.range(...)` loop. `asc2.range` accepts ONLY `unroll_factor` and\n  `parallel` — there is NO `gm_barrier` kwarg on this build (it raises\n  TypeError).\n- Cross-core reductions (VERIFIED): `asc2.atomic_add(src_tile, dst_gm,\n  [offset])` atomically accumulates a tile into global memory (dtypes int16/\n  int32/f16/bf16/f32; also `asc2.atomic_max`). Host must zero the\n  destination first (`torch.zeros(...)` — tensor creation is allowed).\n  Pattern: each core reduce_sums its tiles into a scalar, widens it with\n  `asc2.full([8], s, dtype=...)`, and atomic_adds slot [0]; a second tiny\n  kernel (or the same one on one core) applies any final transform.\n- Scalar reduction results must be widened before store:\n  `asc2.copy_out(asc2.full([8], s, dtype=...), out_gm, [0], real_shape=[8])`\n  style (min 32 bytes).\n- Inside `@asc2.jit`: NO `print`, NO imports, NO `break`/`continue`/early\n  `return`, NO exceptions, NO Python `range()` over runtime values (use\n  `asc2.range`), NO `math.*` calls (precompute module-level constants).\n\n## Numerical stability (MANDATORY — f32 cases use ranges like [-88, 88] and [-100, 100] under a ~1.2e-4 relative-error threshold)\n\n- Never let `exp()` see a positive argument that can overflow; never subtract\n  nearly-equal quantities (catastrophic cancellation); never rely on\n  `log(1 + tiny)` (flushes to 0 below tiny < 6e-8).\n- Proven cancellation-free building blocks (all verified on this harness):\n  - `sigmoid(s) = exp(min(s, 0)) / (1 + exp(-|s|))`\n  - `1 + tanh(u) = 2 * sigmoid(2u)`\n  - `tanh(softplus(x))`: with `w = exp(-|x|)`, equals\n    `(1 + 2w) / (1 + 2w + 2w^2)` for `x >= 0`, `(w^2 + 2w) / (w^2 + 2w + 2)`\n    for `x < 0` (exact identities; blend with `asc2.where(xf >= 0.0, ...)`)\n  - `erfc(z)` for `z >= 0`: Numerical Recipes fit `t * exp(-z*z + P(t))`,\n    `t = 1/(1 + z/2)`, rel. err < 1.2e-7 (see the gelu reference module for\n    the 9-coefficient Horner chain)\n- IEEE special values (inf/nan scalars or extreme inputs) propagate correctly\n  through the hardware ops — do NOT special-case them with host branches\n  unless the golden does.\n\n## Anti-cheat (violations zero the submission)\n\n- ALL numerical work happens inside `@asc2.jit` kernels launched on the NPU.\n- torch usage is allowed ONLY for: output allocation (`torch.empty`,\n  `torch.empty_like`), metadata (`.shape`, `.numel()`, `.stride()`, `.dtype`,\n  `.is_contiguous()`), contiguity (`.contiguous()`), and views (`.view`,\n  `.reshape`, `.narrow`, indexing that returns a view).\n- FORBIDDEN anywhere in the module: torch math/compute ops (`torch.mul`,\n  `torch.norm`, `torch.nn.functional.*`, tensor arithmetic like `a + b`,\n  `x.sigmoid()`, `.to(dtype)` casts of device data, `torch.cat`,\n  `torch.clone`, `torch.sum`, ...). The harness hooks torch dispatch and\n  rotates input data pointers between calls — caching outputs by `data_ptr`\n  is detected and scored as cheating.\n- Outputs must be contiguous NPU tensors with exactly the golden's\n  shape/dtype. Do not return views of inputs.\n\n\n# Operator-specific guidance\n\n-\n\n# Deliverable\n\nWrite ONLY `candidate.py` (complete, self-contained module). Public callable named exactly `mish` with the exact schema signature including attr defaults. Think hard about numerical stability across the full value ranges listed above, and about the UB budget for your op chain before picking TILE.\n\nIMPORTANT — no local execution: pyasc/asc/asc2/torch_npu are NOT installed on this machine and there is no NPU here. Do NOT run, import, compile-check, or test your code, and do not install packages — any such attempt wastes your entire time budget. Reason statically, write `candidate.py`, optionally run `python3 -m py_compile candidate.py` (syntax only), then STOP and reply DONE.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":431,"totalLines":431,"truncated":false}},"title":"integrations/cannbench/workers/.scratch/20260902_140812/mish-generate/task.md","time":{"start":1788347529954,"end":1788347529970}},"id":"prt_061d1b886001xSW5LD52LwZGdE","sessionID":"ses_f9e2e5412ffeyD0ZjwOyLPIQbA","messageID":"msg_061d1acfe001tJtGe14w5Ev3Fw"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788347530715,"sessionID":"ses_f9e2e5412ffeyD0ZjwOyLPIQbA","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_d98f079da61e4ee0b8f43c30","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/workers/.scratch/20260902_140812/mish-generate/design.md"},"output":"<path>/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/workers/.scratch/20260902_140812/mish-generate/design.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Mish Operator Design\n2: \n3: ## Algorithm\n4: \n5: `mish(x) = x * tanh(softplus(x))` where `softplus(x) = ln(1 + e^x)`.\n6: \n7: Use the **cancellation-free** identity for `tanh(softplus(x))` (from task.md):\n8: \n9: With `w = exp(-|x|)`:\n10: - **x >= 0**: `tanh_sp = (1 + 2w) / (1 + 2w + 2w^2)`\n11: - **x < 0**: `tanh_sp = (w^2 + 2w) / (w^2 + 2w + 2)`\n12: \n13: Then `y = x * tanh_sp`. No `exp()` ever sees a positive argument; no `log(1+tiny)` appears.\n14: \n15: ## Pinned-v2 APIs\n16: \n17: | Concern | Pinned API |\n18: |---------|-----------|\n19: | Global views | `asc2.global_tensor(ptr, [size])` |\n20: | Load | `asc2.copy_in(gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])` |\n21: | Store | `asc2.copy_out(tile, gm, [off], real_shape=[n])` |\n22: | Tile loop | `asc2.range(start, stop, step, unroll_factor=2)` — NO `parallel`, NO `gm_barrier` |\n23: | Launch | `kernel[cores](...)`, `cores = min(72, num_tiles)` |\n24: | ConstExpr | `tile_size: asc.ConstExpr[int]` for copy shape |\n25: | Dtypes | Promote `xf = x.to(asc.float32)`, cast back `y.to(x.dtype)` |\n26: | Element-wise | `asc2.abs`, `asc2.exp`, `asc2.where`, `tile >= 0.0`, arithmetic `+ - * /` |\n27: | Runtime | `ensure_npu_platform()` before any NPU op |\n28: \n29: All scalar operands on the RIGHT of tile operators (`tile + 1.0`, never `1.0 + tile`).\n30: \n31: ## All 20 Cases Coverage\n32: \n33: | Metric | Coverage |\n34: |--------|----------|\n35: | dtypes | f16 (cases 1,4,7,10,14,17), f32 (2,5,8,11,13,15,18,20), bf16 (3,6,9,12,16,19) |\n36: | ranks | 1D (12), 2D (1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,10,15,16,17), 3D (9,18,19), 4D (11), 5D (13,14,20) |\n37: | shapes | Contiguous + non-power-of-2 (1023, 1009, 1021, 363, 367, 373, 8193, 4001, 1000003) |\n38: | values | Tiny ([-0.1,0.1]), moderate ([-1,1]), wide ([-65504,65504], [-1000,1000], [-inf,inf], nan) |\n39: | edges | All-zero (14), inf/-inf (12), all-NaN (13), max-f16 range (10,17) |\n40: \n41: **Strategy**: flatten to 1D (`x.numel()`), single kernel dispatch. Shape/dtype preserved via `torch.empty_like(x)` host-side. All 20 cases route through one code path — no specialization.\n42: \n43: ## Tiling\n44: \n45: - **TILE = 1024** (primary) — fits UB budget for the Mish chain (see below).\n46: - **Grid-stride**: `for t in asc2.range(block_idx, num_tiles, block_num, unroll_factor=2)`\n47: - **Tails**: `n = tile_size if off + tile_size <= size else size - off`; passed as `real_shape=[n]`.\n48: - **Core dispatch**: `cores = min(72, num_tiles)`. All cases have > 970 tiles (min numel ~1M), so 72 cores always saturated.\n49: \n50: ## UB Budget\n51: \n52: 15 visible f32 tiles in the compute chain:\n53: \n54: ```\n55: xf          x.to(f32)\n56: abs_xf      asc2.abs(xf)\n57: neg_abs     -abs_xf\n58: w           asc2.exp(neg_abs)\n59: w2          w * w\n60: two_w       w + w\n61: two_w2      w2 + w2\n62: pos_num     two_w + 1.0\n63: pos_den     pos_num + two_w2\n64: pos_th      pos_num / pos_den\n65: neg_num     w2 + two_w\n66: neg_den     neg_num + 2.0\n67: neg_th      neg_num / neg_den\n68: th          asc2.where(cond, pos_th, neg_th)\n69: y           xf * th\n70: ```\n71: \n72: Plus 1 bool tile (`xf >= 0.0`) — negligible cost (1 byte/element).\n73: \n74: **Measured UB model**: `15 * 4 * TILE * unroll(2) * 1.6x = 192 * TILE`\n75: \n76: | TILE | Estimated UB | Fits 253952? |\n77: |------|-------------|--------------|\n78: | 512 | 98,304 B | Yes |\n79: | 1024 | 196,608 B | Yes |\n80: | 2048 | 393,216 B | No |\n81: \n82: **Selected TILE = 1024.** If UB overflow at compile time, fall back to 512.\n83: \n84: ## Numerical Risks & Mitigations\n85: \n86: | Risk | Mitigation |\n87: |------|-----------|\n88: | `exp(x)` overflow for x > 88 (f32) / x > 11 (f16) | Never called with positive arg; always `exp(-\\|x\\|)` with `-` sign |\n89: | `log(1 + tiny)` flushing to 0 | Never called; algebraic cancellation eliminates `ln` |\n90: | Catastrophic cancellation in subtraction | No subtraction of near-equal quantities in the formulas |\n91: | IEEE special values (inf, NaN, -0) | Propagate naturally: w=exp(-\\|inf\\|)=0 yields correct limits; NaN arithmetic yields NaN |\n92: | Large x (e.g., x=65504 in f16) | w underflows to 0, result = x * 1.0 = x — exact |\n93: | x = -inf | w = 0, num = 0, den = 2, th = 0, y = -inf * 0 = NaN. Matches golden (IEEE). |\n94: | x = +inf | w = 0, num = 1, den = 1, th = 1, y = inf * 1 = inf. Matches golden. |\n95: | x = NaN | All ops propagate NaN. Matches golden. |\n96: | Precision thresholds | f16: 2^-10, bf16: 2^-7, f32: 2^-13. The cancellation-free formulas have relative error well within these bounds since all intermediate quantities remain O(1) or smoothly bounded. |\n97: \n98: ## Anti-Cheat Constraints\n99: \n100: | Rule | Compliance |\n101: |------|-----------|\n102: | All numerics in `@asc2.jit` kernel | Yes — Mish math entirely in kernel |\n103: | No `torch.*` compute ops | No torch.mul, torch.nn.functional, tensor arithmetic, .sigmoid(), .to(dtype) on data |\n104: | torch used only for alloc/metadata/view | `torch.empty_like(x)`, `.numel()`, `.is_contiguous()`, `.contiguous()`, `x.dtype` only |\n105: | No output caching by `data_ptr` | Fresh `torch.empty_like` each call |\n106: | Output shape/dtype matches golden exactly | `torch.empty_like(x)` ensures this |\n107: | Contiguous NPU tensors returned | `torch.empty_like` returns contiguous; kernel writes contiguous |\n108: | `ensure_npu_platform()` called first | Yes, first line of `mish()` wrapper |\n109: \n110: ## Local Validation Ladder\n111: \n112: 1. **Syntax gate**: `python3 -m py_compile candidate.py` — pure Python AST check.\n113: 2. **Static contract review**: verify all pinned-v2 APIs, no forbidden syntax (no `break`, `continue`, `return`, `print`, `import` inside JIT; `asc2.range` not `range`; scalars on right; `ConstExpr` for tile_size).\n114: 3. **Exact-v2 local compile gate**: invoke the local compile harness per `pyasc-cannbench-kernel` skill references. Compile failure = measured feedback → fix and retry. Never drop cases.\n115: 4. **Evidence label**: result is `verified-local-compile` at best until camodel/cannbench evidence arrives.\n116: \n117: DESIGN_DONE\n\n(End of file - total 117 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Mish Operator Design\n\n## Algorithm\n\n`mish(x) = x * tanh(softplus(x))` where `softplus(x) = ln(1 + e^x)`.\n\nUse the **cancellation-free** identity for `tanh(softplus(x))` (from task.md):\n\nWith `w = exp(-|x|)`:\n- **x >= 0**: `tanh_sp = (1 + 2w) / (1 + 2w + 2w^2)`\n- **x < 0**: `tanh_sp = (w^2 + 2w) / (w^2 + 2w + 2)`\n\nThen `y = x * tanh_sp`. No `exp()` ever sees a positive argument; no `log(1+tiny)` appears.\n\n## Pinned-v2 APIs\n\n| Concern | Pinned API |\n|---------|-----------|\n| Global views | `asc2.global_tensor(ptr, [size])` |\n| Load | `asc2.copy_in(gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])` |","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/workers/.scratch/20260902_140812/mish-generate/design.md","text":"# Mish Operator Design\n\n## Algorithm\n\n`mish(x) = x * tanh(softplus(x))` where `softplus(x) = ln(1 + e^x)`.\n\nUse the **cancellation-free** identity for `tanh(softplus(x))` (from task.md):\n\nWith `w = exp(-|x|)`:\n- **x >= 0**: `tanh_sp = (1 + 2w) / (1 + 2w + 2w^2)`\n- **x < 0**: `tanh_sp = (w^2 + 2w) / (w^2 + 2w + 2)`\n\nThen `y = x * tanh_sp`. No `exp()` ever sees a positive argument; no `log(1+tiny)` appears.\n\n## Pinned-v2 APIs\n\n| Concern | Pinned API |\n|---------|-----------|\n| Global views | `asc2.global_tensor(ptr, [size])` |\n| Load | `asc2.copy_in(gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])` |\n| Store | `asc2.copy_out(tile, gm, [off], real_shape=[n])` |\n| Tile loop | `asc2.range(start, stop, step, unroll_factor=2)` — NO `parallel`, NO `gm_barrier` |\n| Launch | `kernel[cores](...)`, `cores = min(72, num_tiles)` |\n| ConstExpr | `tile_size: asc.ConstExpr[int]` for copy shape |\n| Dtypes | Promote `xf = x.to(asc.float32)`, cast back `y.to(x.dtype)` |\n| Element-wise | `asc2.abs`, `asc2.exp`, `asc2.where`, `tile >= 0.0`, arithmetic `+ - * /` |\n| Runtime | `ensure_npu_platform()` before any NPU op |\n\nAll scalar operands on the RIGHT of tile operators (`tile + 1.0`, never `1.0 + tile`).\n\n## All 20 Cases Coverage\n\n| Metric | Coverage |\n|--------|----------|\n| dtypes | f16 (cases 1,4,7,10,14,17), f32 (2,5,8,11,13,15,18,20), bf16 (3,6,9,12,16,19) |\n| ranks | 1D (12), 2D (1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,10,15,16,17), 3D (9,18,19), 4D (11), 5D (13,14,20) |\n| shapes | Contiguous + non-power-of-2 (1023, 1009, 1021, 363, 367, 373, 8193, 4001, 1000003) |\n| values | Tiny ([-0.1,0.1]), moderate ([-1,1]), wide ([-65504,65504], [-1000,1000], [-inf,inf], nan) |\n| edges | All-zero (14), inf/-inf (12), all-NaN (13), max-f16 range (10,17) |\n\n**Strategy**: flatten to 1D (`x.numel()`), single kernel dispatch. Shape/dtype preserved via `torch.empty_like(x)` host-side. All 20 cases route through one code path — no specialization.\n\n## Tiling\n\n- **TILE = 1024** (primary) — fits UB budget for the Mish chain (see below).\n- **Grid-stride**: `for t in asc2.range(block_idx, num_tiles, block_num, unroll_factor=2)`\n- **Tails**: `n = tile_size if off + tile_size <= size else size - off`; passed as `real_shape=[n]`.\n- **Core dispatch**: `cores = min(72, num_tiles)`. All cases have > 970 tiles (min numel ~1M), so 72 cores always saturated.\n\n## UB Budget\n\n15 visible f32 tiles in the compute chain:\n\n```\nxf          x.to(f32)\nabs_xf      asc2.abs(xf)\nneg_abs     -abs_xf\nw           asc2.exp(neg_abs)\nw2          w * w\ntwo_w       w + w\ntwo_w2      w2 + w2\npos_num     two_w + 1.0\npos_den     pos_num + two_w2\npos_th      pos_num / pos_den\nneg_num     w2 + two_w\nneg_den     neg_num + 2.0\nneg_th      neg_num / neg_den\nth          asc2.where(cond, pos_th, neg_th)\ny           xf * th\n```\n\nPlus 1 bool tile (`xf >= 0.0`) — negligible cost (1 byte/element).\n\n**Measured UB model**: `15 * 4 * TILE * unroll(2) * 1.6x = 192 * TILE`\n\n| TILE | Estimated UB | Fits 253952? |\n|------|-------------|--------------|\n| 512 | 98,304 B | Yes |\n| 1024 | 196,608 B | Yes |\n| 2048 | 393,216 B | No |\n\n**Selected TILE = 1024.** If UB overflow at compile time, fall back to 512.\n\n## Numerical Risks & Mitigations\n\n| Risk | Mitigation |\n|------|-----------|\n| `exp(x)` overflow for x > 88 (f32) / x > 11 (f16) | Never called with positive arg; always `exp(-\\|x\\|)` with `-` sign |\n| `log(1 + tiny)` flushing to 0 | Never called; algebraic cancellation eliminates `ln` |\n| Catastrophic cancellation in subtraction | No subtraction of near-equal quantities in the formulas |\n| IEEE special values (inf, NaN, -0) | Propagate naturally: w=exp(-\\|inf\\|)=0 yields correct limits; NaN arithmetic yields NaN |\n| Large x (e.g., x=65504 in f16) | w underflows to 0, result = x * 1.0 = x — exact |\n| x = -inf | w = 0, num = 0, den = 2, th = 0, y = -inf * 0 = NaN. Matches golden (IEEE). |\n| x = +inf | w = 0, num = 1, den = 1, th = 1, y = inf * 1 = inf. Matches golden. |\n| x = NaN | All ops propagate NaN. Matches golden. |\n| Precision thresholds | f16: 2^-10, bf16: 2^-7, f32: 2^-13. The cancellation-free formulas have relative error well within these bounds since all intermediate quantities remain O(1) or smoothly bounded. |\n\n## Anti-Cheat Constraints\n\n| Rule | Compliance |\n|------|-----------|\n| All numerics in `@asc2.jit` kernel | Yes — Mish math entirely in kernel |\n| No `torch.*` compute ops | No torch.mul, torch.nn.functional, tensor arithmetic, .sigmoid(), .to(dtype) on data |\n| torch used only for alloc/metadata/view | `torch.empty_like(x)`, `.numel()`, `.is_contiguous()`, `.contiguous()`, `x.dtype` only |\n| No output caching by `data_ptr` | Fresh `torch.empty_like` each call |\n| Output shape/dtype matches golden exactly | `torch.empty_like(x)` ensures this |\n| Contiguous NPU tensors returned | `torch.empty_like` returns contiguous; kernel writes contiguous |\n| `ensure_npu_platform()` called first | Yes, first line of `mish()` wrapper |\n\n## Local Validation Ladder\n\n1. **Syntax gate**: `python3 -m py_compile candidate.py` — pure Python AST check.\n2. **Static contract review**: verify all pinned-v2 APIs, no forbidden syntax (no `break`, `continue`, `return`, `print`, `import` inside JIT; `asc2.range` not `range`; scalars on right; `ConstExpr` for tile_size).\n3. **Exact-v2 local compile gate**: invoke the local compile harness per `pyasc-cannbench-kernel` skill references. Compile failure = measured feedback → fix and retry. Never drop cases.\n4. **Evidence label**: result is `verified-local-compile` at best until camodel/cannbench evidence arrives.\n\nDESIGN_DONE","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":117,"totalLines":117,"truncated":false}},"title":"integrations/cannbench/workers/.scratch/20260902_140812/mish-generate/design.md","time":{"start":1788347530698,"end":1788347530710}},"id":"prt_061d1bb3f0011qhtSXmiRoFz78","sessionID":"ses_f9e2e5412ffeyD0ZjwOyLPIQbA","messageID":"msg_061d1acfe001tJtGe14w5Ev3Fw"}}
